000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.    SSTRRCV.
000400 AUTHOR.        LYNN M BUNN/ C HILLES.
000500 DATE-WRITTEN.  FEBRUARY 1984.
000600*INSTALLATION.  GOODYEAR.
000700*REMARKS.
000800*
000900*     R E C E I P T    I N T O    S T O R E R O O M
001000*
001100*     MAIN STOREROOM EXEC PROGRAM
001200*
001300*          THIS PROGRAM IS THE STOREROOM PROGRAM WHICH
001400*     CONTROLS BOTH OF THE PREVIOUS STOREROOM MODULES
001500*     (TOKRS & TMODRS).  NOW, 'SR' WILL BE TYPED REGARDLESS
001600*     IF THE RECEIPT INTO THE STOREROOM NEEDS TO BE MODIFIED,
001700*     OR THE RECEIPT IS CORRECT AS IS.  THIS PROGRAM HAS THE
001800*     OPTION OF CALLING THE FOLLOWING SUB-PROGRAMS, DEPENDING
001900*     ON THE USER'S RESPONSE.
002000*
002100*          TINQRSI, TSCRPRNT
002200*
002300*     PROCESSING OUTLINE:
002400*     1.  THE SCREEN ASKS FOR THE RECEIVING SLIP NUMBER
002500*         THE ITEMS WHICH MIGHT NEED TO BE CORRECTED.
002600*     2.  THE USER DECIDES WHETHER THE RECEIVING SLIP CAN BE
002700*         MOVED INTO THE STOREROOM AS IS, OR MUST BE CORRECTED.
002800*     3.  IF THE RECEIVING SLIP MUST BE CORRECTED, A SECOND
002900*         SCREEN IS SHOWN WITH ALL LOCATIONS (PER CORP CODE).
003000*     4.  UPDATE THE DATA-BASE.
003100*         MPORCV                 f1  - "XX"
003200*                                f2  - "MM".
003300*         DPOITEM (ACCUM & RCV)  STORED AMOUNT, DATE STORED.
003400*         MSTORERM               STR-ONHAND, NEW LOCATION
003500*                                INDIVIDUAL LOCATION'S ONHAND,
003600*                                ACTIVITY DATE.
003700*         DDAILYTC               325: UNIT PRICE, AMOUNT STORED,
003800*                                     STR-UM.
003900*         (NO TRANSACTION IS CUT IF THE QUANTITY IS ZERO.)
004000*
004100*     5.  NO PRINT-OUT GENERATED.
004200*
004300**   FEBRUARY 1, 1984, THE PROGRAM WAS STILL BEING DEVELOPED,
004400*        AND ITEM LOCKING FORM MSTORERM WAS ADDED.  LMB.
004500*
004600*    FEBRUARY 17, 1984, DAN REQUESTED THAT I MOVE SPACES BACK
004700*        TO THE ITEMS ON THE FIRST SCREEN IF THE USER HAS AN
004800*        ERROR.  (FIELD EDITS MOVES ZEROES INTO THE ITEMS).
004900*        LMB.
005000*
005100*    FEBRUARY 27, 1984, LEROY THOMPSON REQUESTED TWO SMALL CHANGES
005200*        TO FURTHER HELP THE USERS.  LMB.
005300*
005400*    ON JULY 13, 1984, FIXED A BUG RELATING TO KELLY PLANTS.
005500*    ANY TIME THE PROGRAM CAME UPON A KELLY RCV SLIP NUMBER
005600*    WITH THE LAST 3 DIGITS ZEROES (LIKE 24000), THE PROGRAM
005700*    WOULD GO INTO AN INFINITE LOOP UPDATING DPOITEM
005800*    DETAILS.  THIS WAS FIXED.  ALSO PREVENTED ZEROS FROM
005900*    FILLING THE SCREEN WHEN A PROGRAM EDIT (AS OPPOSED TO
006000*    VIEW EDIT) IS HIT BY USING THE "FINISHFORM" CALL TO
006100*    STRIP ZEROS AND LEFT SHIFT NUMERIC FIELDS.
006200*    ALSO CLEANED UP CODE - GETTING RID OF UNNEEDED LOGIC,
006300*    AND ADDED A CALL TO "TBLOWUP" TO HANDLE FATAL ERROR
006400*    CONDITIONS (IN PUB SL - THUS ";LIB=P PARAMETER MUST
006500*    BE USED).  CIH.
006600*
006700*    ON AUGUST 1, 1984, FIXED ANOTHER BUG THAT WAS
006800*    DISCOVERED.  IF A CODE WAS ORDERED IN STOREROOM UM,
006900*    THEN RECEIVED IN AN ALTERNATE UM WHICH WAS A FRACTION
007000*    OF 1 STOREROOM UM (IE STR UM = "BX", ALT UM = "EA",
007100*    ORD 64 BX, RCVD 21 EA = .84 BX) THEN THE UPDATE OF
007200*    QUANTITY ADDED TO STOREROOM DID NOT GET ROUNDED, IT
007300*    GOT TRUNCATED.  THIS RESULTED IN AN INCORRECT ONHAND
007400*    FIGURE AND AN INABILITY TO CORRECT THE PROBLEM WITH
007500*    "MR2" - CORRECT RCV SLIP INTO STOREROOM.  FIXED THE
007600*    ROUNDING PROBLEM.  CIH.
007700*
007800*    ON AUGUST 2, 1984, ADDED THE ABILITY TO CALL RECEIVING
007900*    SLIP INQUIRY FOR KELLY PLANTS FROM THE f7 KEY.  THIS
008000*    INVOLVED A CHANGE TO THE RECEIVING SLIP INQUIRY SUB-
008100*    PROGRAM "TINQRSI" TO MAKE IT WORK FOR THE SPECIAL
008200*    KELLY RECEIVING SLIP NUMBERS.  CIH.
008300*
008400*    ON AUGUST 7, 1984, ANOTHER BUG WAS DISCOVERED.  THE
008500*    TABLE OF ITEMS WAS 24 ELEMENTS, AND A RECEIVING SLIP
008600*    WAS ENCOUNTERED WITH MORE THAN 24 ITEMS.  UPPED THIS
008700*    TABLE TO 100.  CIH.
008800*
008900*    ON JULY 28, 1985,  THIS PROGRAM WAS MODIFIED TO DISALLOW
009000*    THE PROCESSING OF CODES FROZEN FOR INVENTORY.  IF THE
009100*    USER CHOOSES TO ACCEPT THE SLIP AS IS AND A CODE IS
009200*    FROZEN THE ENTIRE SLIP WILL BE REJECTED.
009300*    WHEN THE USER SELECTS TO MODIFY ENTRIES ONLY THE ITEMS
009400*    FROZEN ARE DISALLOWED.      D. HOERLE.
009500*
009600*    ON SEPTEMBER 17, 1985 - CHANGED THE DDAILYTC 325 TO INCLUDE
009700*    THE KELLY RECEIVER'S SEQUENCE NUMBER AT THE END OF THE TC.
009800*    -BARBARA WINTER.
009900*
010000*    ON OCTOBER 7, 1985 - UPDATED THE RECEIVING SLIP INQUIRY IN
010100*    THIS PROGRAM TO CALL THE CURRENT VERSION AND TO USE THE
010200*    FORMFILE FROM THE INQUIRY INSTEAD OF AN OLD VERSION THAT
010300*    WAS COMPILED WITH THIS PROGRAM.  - BARBARA WINTER.
010400*
010500*   10/08/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND
010600*             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE
010700*             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND
010800*             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.
010900*   10/08/85  CHANGED ALL REFERENCES OF TSCRPRNT TO TSCRPRT2,
011000*             TDATECHK TO TDATECK2.
011100*             THIS WAS TO INCORPORATE THE NATIVE LANGUAGE
011200*             SUPPORT VERSIONS OF THESE SUBROUTINES.
011300*                              -TW COTTON.
011400*
011500*    02/13/86.
011600*      CHANGED THIS PROGRAM TO A SUBPROGRAM SO IT MAY BE CALLED
011700*      FROM THE NEW STORES EXECUTIVE PROGRAM "TUDCSTR".  CIH.
      *C
      *C  11/22/93    JEFF BUNGO REQUEST 4502
      *C     ADDED PARAMETER SET TO SPACES TO CALL TO SINQRSI.  PARM
      *C     WAS ADDED FOR INQUIRIES TO HISTORY.  THE INQUIRY FROM
      *C     THIS PROGRAM WILL BE FOR LIVE DB ONLY.
      *C
      *C  09/19/94    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     WRITE TRANSACTION 341 IF THE ITEM BEING RECEIVED INTO
      *C     THE STOREROOM HAS A CHAT NUMBER ASSIGNED TO IT.  THE
      *C     TC 341 WILL BE PASSED TO THE CHESS CORPORATE SYSTEM.
      *C
      *C  08/15/95    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     ALLOW KELLY PLANTS TO ENTER EITHER THE CSIS RECEIVING
      *C     SLIP NUMBER OR THE KELLY RECEIVING SLIP PRAPS NUMBER.
      *C
      *C  04/10/96    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     CHANGE DIRECT DELIVERY CHECK FROM CHECKING DD IN DATE
      *C     STORED TO USE THE CDDCHECK SUBROUTINE.  THE PO HEADER
      *C     ITEM HAD TO BE RETRIEVED BEFORE THE SUBROUTINE WAS
      *C     CALLED.
      *C
      *C  06/06/96    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C
      *C  01/13/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXTENDED TABLE OF ITEMS TO 1000 TO ALLOW FOR MAXIMUM
      *C     NUMBER OF ITEMS ALLOWED ON A RECEIVING SLIP.
      *C
      *C  04/28/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     ADDED LOGIC FOR FRANCHISED OWNED CODES.  IF A CODE IS
      *C     FRANCHISED OWNED AND THE VENDOR CODE ON THE PO IS A
      *C     FRANCHISE VENDOR THEN RECEIPT INTO THE STOREROOM SHOULD
      *C     BE DONE INTO THE PRIMARY FRANCHISE BIN ON "ACCEPT AS IS".
      *C     EDIT ON RECEIPT INTO BINS (F2) THAT RECEIPT IS BEING DONE
      *C     INTO A FRANCHISE BIN.  IF PO FRANCHISE IS NOT THE SAME AS
      *C     THE CODE FRANCHISE THEN RECEIPT SHOULD BE DONE INTO A
      *C     GOODYEAR BIN.
      *C
      *C  09/03/97    JEFF BUNGO
      *C     IF STORES RECEIPTS INTERFACE WITH AN EXTERNAL SYSTEM
      *C     (APPLICATION), CALL THE EXTERNAL STORES INTERFACE
      *C     PROGRAM TO PASS THE DATA.
      *C
      *C  03/07/02    CA YODER
      *C     NAPANEE REPORTED THAT THE BIN LOCATIONS WERE NOT BEING
      *C     UPDATED ALONG WITH THE ONHAND QTY WHEN "F1" PRESSED.
      *C     FOUND THAT THERE WAS AN INCORRECTLY-PLACED PERIOD
      *C     IN 9200-ADD-OK-ONHAND PARAGRAPH, CAUSING THE BIN LOGIC
      *C     TO BE SKIPPED.  ALSO MOVED 0 TO SUB IN 9300-DETERMINE-
      *C     MULT-STR-CODE BECAUSE IT WASN'T BEING INITIALIZED BEFORE
      *C     THE LOOP.
      *C
      *C  07/10/03    CA YODER   (NAPANEE REQUEST)
      *C     ADDED LOGIC TO CHECK THE USER-ID ON THE RECEIVING SLIP
      *C     TO MAKE SURE THE SAME PERSON IS NOT PERFORMING BOTH
      *C     THE RECEIVING AND STORING FUNCTIONS.
      *C
011800*
